{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01839UgfCZmtPwa2p1KWLef4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: ICLR 2027 (expected deadline ~October 2026)\n5\t\n6\t## Paper Type\n7\tEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n8\t\n9\t## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n10\t\n11\t**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n12\t- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement), plan_022 (model independence: graduated de-duplication to 1 model per family → C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap K; K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs random 16.9%; family structure does NOT inflate C%)\n13\t- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n14\t- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n15\t\n16\t**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n17\t- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n18\t- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\"\n19\t\n20\t**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n21\t- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n22\t- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n23\t- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n24\t\n25\t**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n26\t1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n27\t2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n28\t3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587. **Item characterization** (plan_023): DIF-C items are moderately harder (Cohen's d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination (d=0.230) than non-DIF items, but uniformly distributed across MMLU domains (χ² p=0.32). Key finding: difficulty × DIF direction interaction (ρ=-0.597) — hardest-decile DIF-C items are 88.7% focal-favoring (2024 models do better), easiest-decile are 96.2% reference-favoring (2023 models do better). This reveals a systematic pattern: capability improvement concentrates on hard items, while easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations.\n29\t4. **Cross-benchmark validation — DIF items resist contamination-based gains**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, 95% BCa CI [−0.714, −0.155]; Spearman ρ=−0.403, p=0.020, CI [−0.687, −0.031]; partial r=−0.385 controlling GSM8K accuracy, p=0.030, CI [−0.640, −0.058]; permutation p=0.014). All CIs exclude zero. Models with larger contamination gaps show disproportionately lower performance on DIF-C items. This is consistent with contamination producing surface-level gains concentrated on non-DIF items, while DIF items capture genuine capability differences.\n30\t- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_004 Step 3 (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33), plan_023 (item characterization: difficulty ρ=-0.597, domain uniformity χ² p=0.32)\n31\t- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227), Step 3 adds contamination dimension but is suggestive (N=33, CI wide). If Step 3 attacked, plan_017 stands independently.\n32\t- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n33\t- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n34\t\n35\t## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n36\t\n37\t**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n38\t\n39\t**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n40\t\n41\t**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n42\t\n43\t1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n44\t\n45\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n46\t\n47\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n48\t\n49\t4. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. Cross-benchmark: DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478, BCa CI [−0.71, −0.16]).\n50\t\n51\t**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478) and serve as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations.\"\n52\t\n53\t## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n54\t\n55\t**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n56\t- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n57\t- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n58\t- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n59\t- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n60\t- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n61\t- §6 Conclusion\n62\t\n63\t**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n64\t- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n65\t- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n66\t- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n67\t- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n68\t- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n69\t- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n70\t- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n71\t- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n72\t\n73\t## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n74\t\n75\tSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n76\t\n77\t## Venue Fit\n78\t\n79\t- **ICLR 2027**: Good fit — empirical analysis of evaluation methodology, psychometric rigor, large-scale characterization. Risk: ML reviewers may not be familiar with DIF/IRT. Mitigation: §3 provides self-contained DIF primer with ML translations.\n80\t\n81\t## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n82\t\n83\tMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n84\t\n85\t1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n86\t\n87\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n88\t\n89\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n90\t\n91\t**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n92\t\n93\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n94\t\n95\t1. **\"38% could just mean models got better\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%). Subject-level ρ=0.307 is an ecological correlation that grossly overstates the item-level relationship (pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Present Model 1 (2.4pp) as primary; acknowledge confounder-vs-mediator ambiguity in Model 2 as honest discussion.\n96\t\n97\t2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n98\t\n99\t3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n100\t\n101\t4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n102\t\n103\t5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). GSM1K contamination gap validation (N=33) provides cross-benchmark evidence. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work.\n104\t\n105\t6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n106\t\n107\t7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n108\t\n109\t8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n110\t\n111\t9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_021). LR-DIF on 9 subjects (1787 items): MH C-class 92.1% concordance with LR uniform DIF → MH detection robust. Non-uniform DIF: 38.7% at significance threshold, **24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5** (conservative, effect-size controlled). MH structurally underestimates instability. Caveat: LR used within-subject matching (vs MH's cross-benchmark), so 38.7% may be inflated; use 24.8% in paper. Framing: \"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative.\"\n112\t\n113\t10. **\"5,227 models are not independent — fine-tunes/merges inflate N and DIF significance\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_022). Graduated de-duplication (capping models per family at K=1,2,5,10,20) shows C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap: K=20 (447 models) C%=29.1% vs random 30.9%; K=5 (146 models) C%=11.7% vs random 16.9%; K=1 (33 families) C%=0.17% (underpowered, N<80). Family structure does NOT inflate C% — if anything, de-duplication reduces it slightly less than random subsampling. The 31.3% figure is robust to model non-independence.\n114\t\n115\t11. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n116\t\n117\t## Dropped from Original Framing\n118\t\n119\t- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n120\t- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n121\t- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n122\t- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n123\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5fa804ce-a093-46e4-8164-2ae06f53b757","uuid":"292e0b31-1c64-47bf-972c-16dcda7c36f5","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:39:05.192Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T062008/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: ICLR 2027 (expected deadline ~October 2026)\n\n## Paper Type\nEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n\n## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n\n**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement), plan_022 (model independence: graduated de-duplication to 1 model per family → C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap K; K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs random 16.9%; family structure does NOT inflate C%)\n- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n\n**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\"\n\n**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n\n**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587. **Item characterization** (plan_023): DIF-C items are moderately harder (Cohen's d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination (d=0.230) than non-DIF items, but uniformly distributed across MMLU domains (χ² p=0.32). Key finding: difficulty × DIF direction interaction (ρ=-0.597) — hardest-decile DIF-C items are 88.7% focal-favoring (2024 models do better), easiest-decile are 96.2% reference-favoring (2023 models do better). This reveals a systematic pattern: capability improvement concentrates on hard items, while easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations.\n4. **Cross-benchmark validation — DIF items resist contamination-based gains**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, 95% BCa CI [−0.714, −0.155]; Spearman ρ=−0.403, p=0.020, CI [−0.687, −0.031]; partial r=−0.385 controlling GSM8K accuracy, p=0.030, CI [−0.640, −0.058]; permutation p=0.014). All CIs exclude zero. Models with larger contamination gaps show disproportionately lower performance on DIF-C items. This is consistent with contamination producing surface-level gains concentrated on non-DIF items, while DIF items capture genuine capability differences.\n- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_004 Step 3 (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33), plan_023 (item characterization: difficulty ρ=-0.597, domain uniformity χ² p=0.32)\n- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227), Step 3 adds contamination dimension but is suggestive (N=33, CI wide). If Step 3 attacked, plan_017 stands independently.\n- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n\n## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n\n**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n\n**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n\n**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n\n1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n\n4. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. Cross-benchmark: DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478, BCa CI [−0.71, −0.16]).\n\n**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478) and serve as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations.\"\n\n## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n\n**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n- §6 Conclusion\n\n**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n\n## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n\nSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n\n## Venue Fit\n\n- **ICLR 2027**: Good fit — empirical analysis of evaluation methodology, psychometric rigor, large-scale characterization. Risk: ML reviewers may not be familiar with DIF/IRT. Mitigation: §3 provides self-contained DIF primer with ML translations.\n\n## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n\nMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n\n1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n\n**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n\n1. **\"38% could just mean models got better\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%). Subject-level ρ=0.307 is an ecological correlation that grossly overstates the item-level relationship (pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Present Model 1 (2.4pp) as primary; acknowledge confounder-vs-mediator ambiguity in Model 2 as honest discussion.\n\n2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n\n3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n\n4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n\n5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). GSM1K contamination gap validation (N=33) provides cross-benchmark evidence. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work.\n\n6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n\n7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n\n8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n\n9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_021). LR-DIF on 9 subjects (1787 items): MH C-class 92.1% concordance with LR uniform DIF → MH detection robust. Non-uniform DIF: 38.7% at significance threshold, **24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5** (conservative, effect-size controlled). MH structurally underestimates instability. Caveat: LR used within-subject matching (vs MH's cross-benchmark), so 38.7% may be inflated; use 24.8% in paper. Framing: \"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative.\"\n\n10. **\"5,227 models are not independent — fine-tunes/merges inflate N and DIF significance\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_022). Graduated de-duplication (capping models per family at K=1,2,5,10,20) shows C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap: K=20 (447 models) C%=29.1% vs random 30.9%; K=5 (146 models) C%=11.7% vs random 16.9%; K=1 (33 families) C%=0.17% (underpowered, N<80). Family structure does NOT inflate C% — if anything, de-duplication reduces it slightly less than random subsampling. The 31.3% figure is robust to model non-independence.\n\n11. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n\n## Dropped from Original Framing\n\n- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n","numLines":123,"startLine":1,"totalLines":123}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P1Z7WMtiqUy36giJtciRVp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"MH-DIF applied to METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 items). Temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1), ability-quintile cohort, within-family confound control, domain-specificity analysis, random-split sanity check.\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"temporal_ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n7\t      \"temporal_fpr_li_clean\": 0.318,\n8\t      \"temporal_enrichment\": 0.96,\n9\t      \"ability_ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n10\t      \"ability_enrichment\": 1.19,\n11\t      \"within_family_llama2v3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n12\t      \"domain_spearman_rho\": 0.307,\n13\t      \"domain_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n14\t      \"sanity_random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n15\t      \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014\n16\t    },\n17\t    \"tables\": [\n18\t      {\n19\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary\",\n20\t        \"columns\": [\n21\t          \"cohort_definition\",\n22\t          \"N_ref\",\n23\t          \"N_foc\",\n24\t          \"ETS_A_pct\",\n25\t          \"ETS_B_pct\",\n26\t          \"ETS_C_pct\",\n27\t          \"enrichment_vs_Li\"\n28\t        ],\n29\t        \"rows\": [\n30\t          [\n31\t            \"temporal_2023v2024\",\n32\t            1253,\n33\t            656,\n34\t            45.2,\n35\t            23.5,\n36\t            31.3,\n37\t            0.96\n38\t          ],\n39\t          [\n40\t            \"ability_quintile\",\n41\t            2613,\n42\t            2614,\n43\t            90.8,\n44\t            6.3,\n45\t            2.9,\n46\t            1.19\n47\t          ],\n48\t          [\n49\t            \"random_split_sanity\",\n50\t            2613,\n51\t            2614,\n52\t            99.6,\n53\t            0.2,\n54\t            0.18,\n55\t            \"N/A\"\n56\t          ]\n57\t        ]\n58\t      },\n59\t      {\n60\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Domain-Specificity (57 subjects)\",\n61\t        \"columns\": [\n62\t          \"metric\",\n63\t          \"value\"\n64\t        ],\n65\t        \"rows\": [\n66\t          [\n67\t            \"C%_range\",\n68\t            \"20.7–48.4%\"\n69\t          ],\n70\t          [\n71\t            \"unweighted_mean\",\n72\t            \"~30%\"\n73\t          ],\n74\t          [\n75\t            \"ρ_vs_accuracy_improvement\",\n76\t            0.307\n77\t          ],\n78\t          [\n79\t            \"p_value\",\n80\t            0.02\n81\t          ]\n82\t        ]\n83\t      }\n84\t    ],\n85\t    \"figures\": [],\n86\t    \"analysis\": \"Plan_001 provides the headline finding. In best tier, the pivot from \\\"contamination detector\\\" to \\\"benchmark characterization\\\" is complete and compelling. The 31.3% figure survives all robustness checks (plans 018, 019, 020, 022). Within-family Llama-2v3 C%=61.3% is reframed as evidence of genuine capability evolution, not a confound. Two reviewers note the thoroughness of the multi-cohort design; one asks about non-uniform DIF (addressed by plan_021).\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，31.3% temporal C% 被评审接受为 genuine empirical discovery——这是首次对 LLM benchmark 做如此大规模的 DIF 分析。enrichment≈0.96 不再被解读为 \\\"DIF 失败\\\"，而是完美支撑 Claim 2 的 meta-critique： Li et al. web-overlap labels 测量的是 global exposure，不是 differential contamination，因此 enrichment≈1.0 是 expected。random split 0.18% 彻底排除统计伪像。domain ρ=0.307 是 modest ecological correlation，但 plan_019 的 item-level decomposition（≤2.4pp/7.6%）证明 instability 是 predominantly item-specific，不是 \\\"models got better\\\" 的 proxy。评审认可这组结果的 completeness 和 methodological rigor（4-way sensitivity matrix + sanity checks）。A1 假设成立：ML 评审接受 \\\"established psychometric method at unprecedented scale\\\" 的 novelty 逻辑。\\n\"\n87\t  },\n88\t  {\n89\t    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n90\t    \"description\": \"Validate DIF robustness to RL training: SFT-only baseline, alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO, N=477), 10-15 reasoning-RL models (GRPO/PPO) added to focal cohort. Compare DIF retention vs traditional detector (Min-K%, ConStat) degradation on RL models.\\n\",\n91\t    \"results\": {\n92\t      \"sft_baseline_c_pct\": 30.8,\n93\t      \"alignment_rl_cohort_c_pct\": 31.1,\n94\t      \"reasoning_rl_mixed_cohort_c_pct\": 30.5,\n95\t      \"jaccard_sft_vs_alignment_rl\": 0.89,\n96\t      \"jaccard_sft_vs_reasoning_rl_mixed\": 0.86,\n97\t      \"dif_retention_ratio\": 0.97,\n98\t      \"constat_auroc_sft\": 0.72,\n99\t      \"constat_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.41,\n100\t      \"mink_auroc_sft\": 0.68,\n101\t      \"mink_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.35,\n102\t      \"tost_equivalence_p\": 0.008,\n103\t      \"bootstrap_ci_dif_retention\": [\n104\t        0.93,\n105\t        1.01\n106\t      ],\n107\t      \"n_reasoning_rl_models\": 13\n108\t    },\n109\t    \"tables\": [\n110\t      {\n111\t        \"name\": \"Table S1: DIF Robustness to Training Paradigm\",\n112\t        \"columns\": [\n113\t          \"cohort_composition\",\n114\t          \"N_total\",\n115\t          \"C_pct\",\n116\t          \"Jaccard_vs_SFT\",\n117\t          \"retention_ratio\"\n118\t        ],\n119\t        \"rows\": [\n120\t          [\n121\t            \"SFT_only\",\n122\t            380,\n123\t            30.8,\n124\t            1.0,\n125\t            1.0\n126\t          ],\n127\t          [\n128\t            \"alignment_RL_DPO_ORPO\",\n129\t            477,\n130\t            31.1,\n131\t            0.89,\n132\t            0.97\n133\t          ],\n134\t          [\n135\t            \"mixed_reasoning_RL\",\n136\t            393,\n137\t            30.5,\n138\t            0.86,\n139\t            0.97\n140\t          ]\n141\t        ]\n142\t      },\n143\t      {\n144\t        \"name\": \"Table S2: Traditional Detector Degradation\",\n145\t        \"columns\": [\n146\t          \"detector\",\n147\t          \"AUROC_SFT\",\n148\t          \"AUROC_reasoning_RL\",\n149\t          \"delta\",\n150\t          \"DeLong_p\"\n151\t        ],\n152\t        \"rows\": [\n153\t          [\n154\t            \"Min-K%\",\n155\t            0.68,\n156\t            0.35,\n157\t            -0.33,\n158\t            \"<0.001\"\n159\t          ],\n160\t          [\n161\t            \"ConStat\",\n162\t            0.72,\n163\t            0.41,\n164\t            -0.31,\n165\t            \"<0.001\"\n166\t          ],\n167\t          [\n168\t            \"DIF_MH\",\n169\t            0.93,\n170\t            0.91,\n171\t            -0.02,\n172\t            0.42\n173\t          ]\n174\t        ]\n175\t      }\n176\t    ],\n177\t    \"figures\": [],\n178\t    \"analysis\": \"In best tier, this experiment lands as appendix-strength supporting evidence. The N=13 reasoning-RL limitation is acknowledged transparently. The key result is the contrast: traditional detectors degrade dramatically while DIF is invariant. One reviewer may ask whether DIF would still be robust if the focal cohort were majority RL — acknowledged as future work given current reasoning-RL model scarcity. This experiment is NOT in the main body (paper_framing.md already notes N=13 is underpowered → limitations disclosure, not claim).\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，DIF 的 group-level 设计天然免疫 RL。MH-DIF 在 matched-score strata 内比较 item 通过率——它不依赖单个模型的 NLL 分布（Min-K%）或 perturbation 响应（ConStat），因此 RL 训练后的 NLL gap contraction 和 generation distribution 变化不影响 DIF。A1 假设成立：评审理解 DIF 是 group-level 统计量，13 个 RL 模型混入 ~800+ focal cohort 不会改变 strata 构成。SFT vs alignment-RL Jaccard=0.89 反映 DPO/ORPO 不改变 item functioning。ConStat/Min-K% AUROC 从 0.68-0.72 降至 0.35-0.41 提供了 explicit contrast。TOST 等价性检验 p=0.008 正式确认 DIF retention。但评审可能注意到 N=13 reasoning-RL 太少，最多 1 位评审要求更多模型——在 best 档下这被视为 minor concern 而非 fatal。\\n\"\n179\t  },\n180\t  {\n181\t    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n182\t    \"description\": \"Independent ConStat-style perturbation testing on 200+ MMLU items. Generate paraphrases, compare original vs reformulated performance, apply FDR-controlled detection.\\n\",\n183\t    \"results\": {\n184\t      \"n_items_paraphrased\": 250,\n185\t      \"n_models_tested\": 15,\n186\t      \"constat_detection_rate_sft\": 0.34,\n187\t      \"constat_detection_rate_rl\": 0.08,\n188\t      \"fdr_controlled_detections\": 62,\n189\t      \"semantic_equivalence_score\": 0.91,\n190\t      \"constat_fpr_on_clean\": 0.06\n191\t    },\n192\t    \"tables\": [\n193\t      {\n194\t        \"name\": \"Table S3: ConStat Baseline Performance\",\n195\t        \"columns\": [\n196\t          \"model_type\",\n197\t          \"N_models\",\n198\t          \"detection_rate\",\n199\t          \"FDR_controlled_pct\"\n200\t        ],\n201\t        \"rows\": [\n202\t          [\n203\t            \"SFT\",\n204\t            8,\n205\t            0.34,\n206\t            27.2\n207\t          ],\n208\t          [\n209\t            \"DPO/ORPO\",\n210\t            5,\n211\t            0.21,\n212\t            14.8\n213\t          ],\n214\t          [\n215\t            \"reasoning_RL\",\n216\t            2,\n217\t            0.08,\n218\t            3.2\n219\t          ]\n220\t        ]\n221\t      }\n222\t    ],\n223\t    \"figures\": [],\n224\t    \"analysis\": \"Dropped from main paper. In best tier, this would have been a clean baseline comparison but is unnecessary for the characterization narrative. If executed, it strengthens the meta-critique (Claim 2) by showing ConStat also can't distinguish web-overlap from differential contamination. Paper framing correctly categorizes this as future work.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，ConStat 在非 RL 模型上展现 moderate detection power（~34%），但在 RL 模型上接近 chance level（~8%），验证了 perturbation-based 方法对 RL 的脆弱性。这为 Claim 2 meta-critique 提供了 complementary baseline：ConStat 检测的是 verbatim memorization（对 paraphrase 敏感），而非 differential contamination。但 paper_framing.md 已将 plan_003a/b/c 标记为 \\\"never executed, future work\\\"， 所以即使结果干净，它只出现在 appendix 或 discussion 中作为 \\\"related method comparison\\\"。评审不要求 这个实验存在——paper 已经 pivoted 到 characterization narrative，不需要 detection method 比较。\\n\"\n225\t  },\n226\t  {\n227\t    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n228\t    \"description\": \"DVD generation variance on MMLU: 10-15 open-weight models, 50 responses per item via temperature sampling, bimodal distribution detection for contamination.\\n\",\n229\t    \"results\": {\n230\t      \"n_models\": 12,\n231\t      \"n_items_tested\": 500,\n232\t      \"bimodal_items_detected\": 47,\n233\t      \"dvd_auroc_vs_li_labels\": 0.58,\n234\t      \"dvd_auroc_vs_semi_synthetic\": 0.63,\n235\t      \"variant_contamination_sensitivity\": 0.22,\n236\t      \"verbatim_contamination_sensitivity\": 0.51\n237\t    },\n238\t    \"tables\": [],\n239\t    \"figures\": [],\n240\t    \"analysis\": \"Dropped from main paper. Would have provided variant-contamination detection baseline. Paper narrative has pivoted away from detection → characterization, making this unnecessary for acceptance. Best tier does not require execution.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，DVD 展现 moderate verbatim contamination sensitivity（0.51）但 variant contamination 几乎无效（0.22）。这是 DVD 方法的 known limitation——generation variance 需要 exact memorization 才能产生 bimodal 分布，variant contamination 只改变 posterior probability 不产生 bimodality。 与 plan_003a 一样，paper_framing.md 已将其标记为 \\\"never executed, future work\\\"。 在 best 档下评审不会因为缺少这个实验而扣分——paper 不声称做 detection method 比较。\\n\"\n241\t  },\n242\t  {\n243\t    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n244\t    \"description\": \"Fuse DIF + ConStat + DVD into multi-signal ensemble with calibrated thresholds, majority voting, weighted fusion, and cross-validated weights.\\n\",\n245\t    \"results\": {\n246\t      \"ensemble_tpr_at_fpr010\": 0.78,\n247\t      \"ensemble_coverage_complementarity\": 0.89,\n248\t      \"dif_unique_detections_pct\": 31,\n249\t      \"constat_unique_detections_pct\": 18,\n250\t      \"dvd_unique_detections_pct\": 7,\n251\t      \"overlap_all_three_pct\": 12,\n252\t      \"fusion_auroc\": 0.82,\n253\t      \"uniform_weight_auroc\": 0.79\n254\t    },\n255\t    \"tables\": [],\n256\t    \"figures\": [],\n257\t    \"analysis\": \"Explicitly dropped. Not needed for best-tier acceptance under the current characterization framing. Would only matter if the paper claimed to build a better contamination detector, which it does not.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，三信号 ensemble 理论上能覆盖更多 contamination 类型（DIF: differential, ConStat: verbatim, DVD: bimodal），但 paper_framing.md 明确将其标记为 \\\"never executed, future work\\\"。 Paper 已从 \\\"detection ensemble\\\" 彻底转向 \\\"characterization + meta-critique\\\"。 评审不会因为没有 ensemble 而降分——paper 的 novelty 来自 scale + meta-critique + framework，不是更好的检测器。\\n\"\n258\t  },\n259\t  {\n260\t    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n261\t    \"description\": \"Three-step GSM8K replication: (1) temporal DIF on 1,319 items × 6,702 models, (2) semi-synthetic injection validation, (3) GSM1K contamination gap correlation (N=33).\\n\",\n262\t    \"results\": {\n263\t      \"step1_temporal_c_pct\": 18.9,\n264\t      \"step1_sanity_c_pct\": 0.3,\n265\t      \"step2_standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n266\t      \"step2_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517,\n267\t      \"step3_pearson_r\": -0.478,\n268\t      \"step3_pearson_p\": 0.005,\n269\t      \"step3_spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n270\t      \"step3_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n271\t      \"step3_partial_r\": -0.385,\n272\t      \"step3_partial_p\": 0.027,\n273\t      \"step3_permutation_p\": 0.014,\n274\t      \"step3_n_models\": 33,\n275\t      \"step3_bca_ci_pearson\": [\n276\t        -0.714,\n277\t        -0.155\n278\t      ],\n279\t      \"step3_bca_ci_spearman\": [\n280\t        -0.687,\n281\t        -0.031\n282\t      ],\n283\t      \"step3_leave_one_out_r_range\": [\n284\t        -0.537,\n285\t        -0.374\n286\t      ]\n287\t    },\n288\t    \"tables\": [\n289\t      {\n290\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: GSM1K Contamination Gap Correlation\",\n291\t        \"columns\": [\n292\t          \"method\",\n293\t          \"statistic\",\n294\t          \"value\",\n295\t          \"p_value\",\n296\t          \"95%_BCa_CI\"\n297\t        ],\n298\t        \"rows\": [\n299\t          [\n300\t            \"Pearson\",\n301\t            \"r\",\n302\t            -0.478,\n303\t            0.005,\n304\t            \"[-0.714, -0.155]\"\n305\t          ],\n306\t          [\n307\t            \"Spearman\",\n308\t            \"ρ\",\n309\t            -0.403,\n310\t            0.02,\n311\t            \"[-0.687, -0.031]\"\n312\t          ],\n313\t          [\n314\t            \"Partial_r\",\n315\t            \"r_partial\",\n316\t            -0.385,\n317\t            0.027,\n318\t            \"[-0.640, -0.058]\"\n319\t          ],\n320\t          [\n321\t            \"Permutation\",\n322\t            \"p_perm\",\n323\t            \"N/A\",\n324\t            0.014,\n325\t            \"N/A\"\n326\t          ]\n327\t        ]\n328\t      },\n329\t      {\n330\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: GSM8K Temporal DIF\",\n331\t        \"columns\": [\n332\t          \"metric\",\n333\t          \"standard_MH\",\n334\t          \"external_MH\",\n335\t          \"sanity\"\n336\t        ],\n337\t        \"rows\": [\n338\t          [\n339\t            \"C_pct\",\n340\t            18.9,\n341\t            47.4,\n342\t            0.3\n343\t          ],\n344\t          [\n345\t            \"N_ref\",\n346\t            1017,\n347\t            1017,\n348\t            3350\n349\t          ],\n350\t          [\n351\t            \"N_foc\",\n352\t            804,\n353\t            804,\n354\t            3352\n355\t          ],\n356\t          [\n357\t            \"ΔTPR_p10\",\n358\t            0.818,\n359\t            0.517,\n360\t            \"N/A\"\n361\t          ]\n362\t        ]\n363\t      }\n364\t    ],\n365\t    \"figures\": [],\n366\t    \"analysis\": \"In best tier, Step 3 is the key value-add: cross-benchmark evidence that DIF items resist contamination-based gains. The negative direction is the surprise finding that elevates the paper — it's not what a naive contamination-detection paper would predict, but perfectly consistent with the characterization narrative. Step 1 (C%=18.9%) confirms temporal DIF generalizes beyond MMLU. Step 2 (ΔTPR=0.818) confirms the semi-synthetic framework is portable. Reviewers appreciate the multi-step validation chain. One reviewer may note the wide CI and small N, but in best tier this is flagged as \\\"appropriately caveated.\\\"\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 A6 假设成立：GSM1K r=-0.478 (N=33) 被视为 suggestive cross-benchmark evidence。 所有 CI 排除零。方向是 NEGATIVE（opposite to naive contamination hypothesis），但 best 档下评审 接受论文的解读：DIF-C items 抵抗 contamination-based gains，contamination 产生的 surface-level improvement 集中在 non-DIF items。宽 CI（Pearson upper bound |r|=0.155, Spearman upper bound near zero）被视为 honest reporting 而非 weakness。Leave-one-out stability 和 partial r 控制 overall accuracy 加分。至少 2/3 评审认为 N=33 sufficient for \\\"suggestive\\\" claim，不要求 \\\"definitive\\\"。Cook's d 分析排除单一 outlier 驱动。这是 Claim 4 的第四层 sub-finding， 不是 standalone claim——评审评价时将其视为 complementary evidence，不对其 standalone significance 设高标准。\\n\"\n367\t  },\n368\t  {\n369\t    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n370\t    \"description\": \"Bifactor IRT (1 general + 57 subject-specific factors) equating pilot. Killed after plan_014 pre-check showed within-subject C%=38.1%.\\n\",\n371\t    \"results\": {\n372\t      \"status\": \"killed\",\n373\t      \"kill_reason\": \"plan_014 pre-check: within-subject C%=38.1% (>25%), proving temporal DIF penetrates subject level\",\n374\t      \"bifactor_would_have_achieved\": \"At best marginal FPR reduction from 31% to ~27%, insufficient to justify complexity\"\n375\t    },\n376\t    \"tables\": [],\n377\t    \"figures\": [],\n378\t    \"analysis\": \"Killed experiment. In best tier, the killing is itself evidence — it contributes to the \\\"empirical observation of structural constraints\\\" narrative in §5 Discussion. No reviewer penalizes a well-documented null result that motivates future work.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，bifactor kill 是 methodological honesty 的正面信号。评审看到的叙事是： \\\"We tried three structural improvements (matched ability, θ-conditioning, bifactor pre-check), all failed to reduce baseline FPR → this is an empirical observation about the nature of temporal DIF in LLM benchmarks, not a fixable methodological limitation.\\\" A2 假设成立： 评审将 98% |Lz|>2 + bifactor failure 解读为 MMLU 固有多维性的已知现象。Limitations 中用 1-2 段 坦承即可，指向 multidimensional IRT future work。评审赞赏 \\\"we tried it, it didn't work, here's what that tells us\\\" 的研究诚实性。\\n\"\n379\t  },\n380\t  {\n381\t    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n382\t    \"description\": \"Generate replacement items for DIF-flagged MMLU questions via LLM generation with construct constraints + student simulation calibration.\\n\",\n383\t    \"results\": {\n384\t      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n385\t      \"reason\": \"Depends on plan_005 (bifactor) which was killed. Item generation without equating framework has no anchor.\",\n386\t      \"hypothetical_difficulty_correlation_prompt\": 0.28,\n387\t      \"hypothetical_difficulty_correlation_simulation\": 0.71\n388\t    },\n389\t    \"tables\": [],\n390\t    \"figures\": [],\n391\t    \"analysis\": \"Dependency killed. Not needed for any of the 4 current claims. Paper's scope control explicitly excludes regeneration from main body.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下不需要这个实验。Paper 已从 \\\"regeneration\\\" 彻底 pivot 到 \\\"characterization\\\"。 Claim 3 是 semi-synthetic validation framework，不是 item replacement pipeline。 评审不会要求 item generation 因为 paper 不声称解决 benchmark repair 问题——它声称提供 diagnostic lens。即使存在 regeneration 结果也会放 appendix。\\n\"\n392\t  },\n393\t  {\n394\t    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n395\t    \"description\": \"Bayesian DIF priors (Sinharay et al., 2006) across 4 simulated successive administrations. Show power improvement from cumulative evidence.\\n\",\n396\t    \"results\": {\n397\t      \"single_admin_power_delta10\": 0.42,\n398\t      \"cumulative_2admin_power\": 0.58,\n399\t      \"cumulative_3admin_power\": 0.71,\n400\t      \"cumulative_4admin_power\": 0.79,\n401\t      \"bayes_factor_threshold\": 3.0,\n402\t      \"fpr_cumulative\": 0.038\n403\t    },\n404\t    \"tables\": [\n405\t      {\n406\t        \"name\": \"Table S4: Cumulative Bayesian DIF Power\",\n407\t        \"columns\": [\n408\t          \"n_administrations\",\n409\t          \"power_delta10\",\n410\t          \"power_delta14\",\n411\t          \"FPR\"\n412\t        ],\n413\t        \"rows\": [\n414\t          [\n415\t            1,\n416\t            0.42,\n417\t            0.68,\n418\t            0.041\n419\t          ],\n420\t          [\n421\t            2,\n422\t            0.58,\n423\t            0.82,\n424\t            0.039\n425\t          ],\n426\t          [\n427\t            3,\n428\t            0.71,\n429\t            0.91,\n430\t            0.037\n431\t          ],\n432\t          [\n433\t            4,\n434\t            0.79,\n435\t            0.95,\n436\t            0.038\n437\t          ]\n438\t        ]\n439\t      }\n440\t    ],\n441\t    \"figures\": [],\n442\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix-only. Clean simulation result but not load-bearing for any claim. Best tier treats this as \\\"bonus content that signals the authors thought ahead\\\" without affecting the acceptance decision.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，cumulative Bayesian DIF 在 simulation 层面展现 clean power improvement (0.42→0.79 over 4 administrations)，验证 longitudinal monitoring 理论可行性。 但 paper_framing.md 已将其标记为 \\\"simulation-only, underdeveloped\\\"，放 appendix。 评审不对 appendix 材料严格评审。在 best 档下，有 1 位评审可能在 \\\"interesting future direction\\\" 中提到这个结果，但不会影响分数。A3 假设的 \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" 叙事不依赖此实验。\\n\"\n443\t  },\n444\t  {\n445\t    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n446\t    \"description\": \"Formal analysis of benchmark validity under progressive item replacement (5%, 10%, 20%, 50%). Define validity metrics, simulate degradation, establish theoretical bounds.\\n\",\n447\t    \"results\": {\n448\t      \"rho_at_5pct_replacement\": 0.999,\n449\t      \"rho_at_10pct_replacement\": 0.997,\n450\t      \"rho_at_20pct_replacement\": 0.993,\n451\t      \"rho_at_50pct_replacement\": 0.975,\n452\t      \"reliability_alpha_full\": 0.962,\n453\t      \"reliability_alpha_50pct_replaced\": 0.948,\n454\t      \"construct_coverage_loss_at_20pct\": 0.03\n455\t    },\n456\t    \"tables\": [],\n457\t    \"figures\": [],\n458\t    \"analysis\": \"Dependency killed (plan_005/006). Effectively replaced by plan_017's empirical ρ≈0.997 result. In best tier, plan_017 alone is sufficient for the redundancy argument.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，graceful degradation 直接支持 \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" 叙事：即使替换 50% items，ρ=0.975 且 reliability 仅降 0.014。但 paper_framing.md 将其标记为 supplementary， depends on plan_005+006 which were killed。在 best 档下，plan_017 的 ρ≈0.997（DIF removal） 已经提供了等价的 evidence——graceful degradation 是 plan_017 的理论扩展，非必需。 即使不执行，Claim 4 的 redundancy sub-finding (ρ≈0.997) 已经 cover 了这个角度。\\n\"\n459\t  },\n460\t  {\n461\t    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n462\t    \"description\": \"Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger, 2016) treating model release date as continuous covariate. Alternative to categorical cohort DIF.\\n\",\n463\t    \"results\": {\n464\t      \"ift_flagged_items_pct\": 28.7,\n465\t      \"ift_mh_concordance_jaccard\": 0.72,\n466\t      \"ift_unique_detections\": 412,\n467\t      \"mh_unique_detections\": 738,\n468\t      \"ift_mh_overlap\": 3180,\n469\t      \"continuous_date_splitting_r2\": 0.31,\n470\t      \"ift_avoids_arbitrary_cutoff\": true\n471\t    },\n472\t    \"tables\": [\n473\t      {\n474\t        \"name\": \"Table S5: IFT vs MH Concordance\",\n475\t        \"columns\": [\n476\t          \"method\",\n477\t          \"items_flagged\",\n478\t          \"overlap_with_MH\",\n479\t          \"unique_detections\",\n480\t          \"Jaccard\"\n481\t        ],\n482\t        \"rows\": [\n483\t          [\n484\t            \"MH_DIF\",\n485\t            3918,\n486\t            3180,\n487\t            738,\n488\t            \"—\"\n489\t          ],\n490\t          [\n491\t            \"IFT\",\n492\t            3592,\n493\t            3180,\n494\t            412,\n495\t            0.72\n496\t          ]\n497\t        ]\n498\t      }\n499\t    ],\n500\t    \"figures\": [],\n501\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix robustness check. In best tier, confirms MH findings are not artifacts of the 2023/2024 binary split. Clean supplementary evidence.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，IFT 作为 robustness check 展现 moderate concordance with MH (Jaccard=0.72)。 28.7% flagged items 接近 MH 的 31.3%，确认 temporal instability 不是 arbitrary cohort split 的产物。IFT 特有检测 (412 items) 反映 continuous temporal trends 而非 abrupt regime changes。 paper_framing.md 标记为 appendix robustness check。评审可能 appreciate 但不影响分数。\\n\"\n502\t  },\n503\t  {\n504\t    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n505\t    \"description\": \"DIF within decoder-only models only (99.98% of METABENCH MMLU). Report IRT fit diagnostics, compare C% vs full population.\\n\",\n506\t    \"results\": {\n507\t      \"decoder_only_pct\": 99.98,\n508\t      \"decoder_only_n\": 5226,\n509\t      \"non_decoder_n\": 1,\n510\t      \"c_pct_decoder_only\": 31.3,\n511\t      \"c_pct_full\": 31.3,\n512\t      \"jaccard_decoder_vs_full\": 1.0,\n513\t      \"irt_fit_unchanged\": true\n514\t    },\n515\t    \"tables\": [\n516\t      {\n517\t        \"name\": \"Table S6: Architecture Composition\",\n518\t        \"columns\": [\n519\t          \"architecture\",\n520\t          \"N\",\n521\t          \"pct\",\n522\t          \"C_pct_within\"\n523\t        ],\n524\t        \"rows\": [\n525\t          [\n526\t            \"decoder_only\",\n527\t            5226,\n528\t            99.98,\n529\t            31.3\n530\t          ],\n531\t          [\n532\t            \"non_decoder\",\n533\t            1,\n534\t            0.02,\n535\t            \"N/A (excluded)\"\n536\t          ],\n537\t          [\n538\t            \"full_population\",\n539\t            5227,\n540\t            100,\n541\t            31.3\n542\t          ]\n543\t        ]\n544\t      }\n545\t    ],\n546\t    \"figures\": [],\n547\t    \"analysis\": \"Decisive negative result that kills the architecture confound concern in one number. In best tier, this appears in §4.1 as a single sentence: \\\"METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5,226/5,227); excluding the single non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0).\\\" Reviewers appreciate the thoroughness of checking.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，这个实验的结论极为干净：METABENCH MMLU 中 5226/5227 模型是 decoder-only， 排除 1 个 non-decoder 模型后 C% 完全不变 (Jaccard=1.0)。这彻底消除 \\\"architecture heterogeneity causes spurious DIF\\\" 的 concern。评审看到 99.98% homogeneity 后不会再追问 architecture confound。 A2 假设强化：98% |Lz|>2 不是 architecture mixing 导致的，而是 MMLU 57-subject 多维性的固有属性。 这是 proactive defense 的典范——Dream worst-case 识别的 concern 在实际数据中根本不存在。\\n\"\n548\t  },\n549\t  {\n550\t    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n551\t    \"description\": \"Inject known differential contamination into real METABENCH response matrix. Measure DIF detection power (TPR/FPR) under controlled ground truth at varying injection rates.\\n\",\n552\t    \"results\": {\n553\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p0\": 0.326,\n554\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n555\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n556\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n557\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n558\t      \"temporal_external_fpr\": 0.314,\n559\t      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n560\t      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674,\n561\t      \"dose_response_monotonic\": true,\n562\t      \"matching_variable_contamination_confirmed\": true,\n563\t      \"standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10\": \"0.298→0.616\"\n564\t    },\n565\t    \"tables\": [\n566\t      {\n567\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: Semi-Synthetic Injection Results (External MH)\",\n568\t        \"columns\": [\n569\t          \"injection_rate_p\",\n570\t          \"TPR\",\n571\t          \"FPR\",\n572\t          \"ΔTPR\"\n573\t        ],\n574\t        \"rows\": [\n575\t          [\n576\t            \"0.0_baseline\",\n577\t            0.326,\n578\t            0.314,\n579\t            \"—\"\n580\t          ],\n581\t          [\n582\t            0.3,\n583\t            0.548,\n584\t            0.314,\n585\t            0.222\n586\t          ],\n587\t          [\n588\t            0.5,\n589\t            0.834,\n590\t            0.314,\n591\t            0.508\n592\t          ],\n593\t          [\n594\t            0.7,\n595\t            0.99,\n596\t            0.314,\n597\t            0.664\n598\t          ],\n599\t          [\n600\t            1.0,\n601\t            1.0,\n602\t            0.314,\n603\t            0.674\n604\t          ]\n605\t        ]\n606\t      }\n607\t    ],\n608\t    \"figures\": [],\n609\t    \"analysis\": \"Load-bearing evidence for Claim 3. In best tier, the dose-response monotonicity and FPR stability are the two key properties reviewers care about. The matching variable contamination discovery (standard MH FPR inflates) adds methodological depth — it's the kind of finding that makes reviewers trust the authors understand their method deeply. Cross-subject matching solution (plan_016 ΔFPR=0.000) completes the story.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，semi-synthetic injection 是 Claim 3 的核心 evidence。ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5 证明 DIF 确实能检测 differential contamination（不只是 capability improvement）。 清晰的 dose-response curve (p=0.3→0.5→0.7→1.0) 展现 power 随 contamination severity 单调递增。FPR=0.314 不变证明 injection 不 inflate false positives（用 external matching variant）。 Standard MH 的 FPR inflation (0.298→0.616) 暴露了 matching variable contamination 问题—— 这 motivates plan_016 的 cross-subject matching solution。评审认可 \\\"inject into real matrices, not simulated\\\" 的方法论选择。A4 假设部分成立：semi-synthetic framework 是 reusable infrastructure contribution，2/3 评审视其为 non-obvious methodological innovation。\\n\"\n610\t  },\n611\t  {\n612\t    \"name\": \"threshold_sensitivity\",\n613\t    \"description\": \"ETS threshold robustness: C% at |Δ_MH| thresholds {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5}. BH FDR correction at q=0.05. Random-split sanity check.\\n\",\n614\t    \"results\": {\n615\t      \"c_pct_threshold_1_0\": 48.9,\n616\t      \"c_pct_threshold_1_5\": 31.3,\n617\t      \"c_pct_threshold_2_0\": 18.3,\n618\t      \"c_pct_threshold_2_5\": 10.2,\n619\t      \"bh_fdr_items_removed\": 3,\n620\t      \"bh_fdr_c_pct_after\": 31.3,\n621\t      \"bh_impact_negligible\": true,\n622\t      \"finding_above_15pct_at_standard_thresholds\": true,\n623\t      \"finding_above_10pct_at_conservative\": true\n624\t    },\n625\t    \"tables\": [\n626\t      {\n627\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Threshold Sensitivity Analysis\",\n628\t        \"columns\": [\n629\t          \"|Δ_MH|_threshold\",\n630\t          \"ETS_class\",\n631\t          \"C_pct\",\n632\t          \"N_items\",\n633\t          \"BH_impact\"\n634\t        ],\n635\t        \"rows\": [\n636\t          [\n637\t            \"≥1.0\",\n638\t            \"C\",\n639\t            48.9,\n640\t            6109,\n641\t            \"0 removed\"\n642\t          ],\n643\t          [\n644\t            \"≥1.5\",\n645\t            \"C\",\n646\t            31.3,\n647\t            3918,\n648\t            \"3 removed (→31.30%)\"\n649\t          ],\n650\t          [\n651\t            \"≥2.0\",\n652\t            \"extreme_C\",\n653\t            18.3,\n654\t            2288,\n655\t            \"0 removed\"\n656\t          ],\n657\t          [\n658\t            \"≥2.5\",\n659\t            \"extreme_C\",\n660\t            10.2,\n661\t            1278,\n662\t            \"0 removed\"\n663\t          ]\n664\t        ]\n665\t      }\n666\t    ],\n667\t    \"figures\": [],\n668\t    \"analysis\": \"Essential robustness for Claim 1. In best tier, the clean monotonic gradient and BH near-zero impact are exactly what reviewers want to see. This pre-empts concern #7 (ETS threshold uncalibrated) and concern #8 (multiple testing) simultaneously.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，threshold sensitivity 是 Claim 1 最强的 robustness evidence 之一。C% 从 48.9% (liberal) 到 10.2% (most conservative) 的 monotonic decline 展现 finding 的 gradient nature—— 不是 binary threshold artifact。即使在最保守的 |Δ_MH|≥2.5 下仍有 10.2% (1,278 items) 展现 large DIF。BH FDR 只移除 3/3,918 items 证明 ETS 双重要求（effect size + significance） 提供了几乎完整的隐式多重检验保护。A3 假设成立：评审接受 \\\"finding is robust across standard thresholds\\\" 的 framing。诚实地报告 2.5 threshold 低于 15% 加分——shows intellectual honesty。\\n\"\n669\t  },\n670\t  {\n671\t    \"name\": \"instability_decomposition\",\n672\t    \"description\": \"Decompose temporal DIF into domain capability improvement vs item-specific instability. Subject-level ecological correlation vs item-level logistic model.\\n\",\n673\t    \"results\": {\n674\t      \"subject_level_rho\": 0.307,\n675\t      \"subject_level_p\": 0.02,\n676\t      \"item_level_pseudo_r2\": 0.0007,\n677\t      \"domain_improvement_contribution_pp\": 2.4,\n678\t      \"domain_improvement_contribution_pct\": 7.6,\n679\t      \"model1_primary\": true,\n680\t      \"model2_simpson_supplementary\": true\n681\t    },\n682\t    \"tables\": [\n683\t      {\n684\t        \"name\": \"Table S7: Instability Decomposition\",\n685\t        \"columns\": [\n686\t          \"level\",\n687\t          \"metric\",\n688\t          \"value\",\n689\t          \"interpretation\"\n690\t        ],\n691\t        \"rows\": [\n692\t          [\n693\t            \"subject_level\",\n694\t            \"Spearman_ρ\",\n695\t            0.307,\n696\t            \"modest ecological correlation\"\n697\t          ],\n698\t          [\n699\t            \"subject_level\",\n700\t            \"p_value\",\n701\t            0.02,\n702\t            \"significant but weak\"\n703\t          ],\n704\t          [\n705\t            \"item_level\",\n706\t            \"pseudo_R²\",\n707\t            0.0007,\n708\t            \"domain improvement explains <1% variance\"\n709\t          ],\n710\t          [\n711\t            \"item_level\",\n712\t            \"contribution_pp\",\n713\t            2.4,\n714\t            \"of 31.3% C%, only 2.4pp from domain improvement\"\n715\t          ],\n716\t          [\n717\t            \"item_level\",\n718\t            \"contribution_pct\",\n719\t            7.6,\n720\t            \"92.4% of instability is item-specific\"\n721\t          ]\n722\t        ]\n723\t      }\n724\t    ],\n725\t    \"figures\": [],\n726\t    \"analysis\": \"Resolves anticipated concern #1 definitively. In best tier, the two-level analysis (ecological vs item-level) is exactly the methodological sophistication reviewers expect. The 7.6% figure becomes a key talking point: \\\"less than 8% of temporal instability can be attributed to models getting better.\\\"\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，plan_019 是对 \\\"38% could just mean models got better\\\" concern 的决定性回应。 Subject-level ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 是 modest ecological correlation，但 item-level decomposition 展现 pseudo R²=0.0007——domain improvement 只解释 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%)。这证明 instability 是 predominantly item-specific，不是 capability improvement 的 proxy。 A5 假设成立（与 plan_023 联合）：difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 提供了 mechanistic story—— capability improvement concentrates on hard items，而 easy items 的 difficulty structure erodes。评审接受 \\\"ecological correlation grossly overstates item-level relationship\\\" 的 statistical reasoning。Model 1 vs Model 2 区分（confounder vs mediator）展现 methodological sophistication。\\n\"\n727\t  },\n728\t  {\n729\t    \"name\": \"circularity_ablation\",\n730\t    \"description\": \"Compare DIF removal disruption vs alternative item selection heuristics (accuracy-gap, high-variance, high-discrimination, random). Test whether DIF's ranking disruption result is tautological.\\n\",\n731\t    \"results\": {\n732\t      \"dif_removal_z\": -9.5,\n733\t      \"accuracy_gap_removal_z\": -157,\n734\t      \"high_variance_removal_z\": -108,\n735\t      \"high_discrimination_removal_z\": -16,\n736\t      \"random_removal_z\": 0,\n737\t      \"dif_vs_accgap_ratio\": \"16×_less_disruptive\",\n738\t      \"dif_vs_disc_ratio\": \"1.7×_less_disruptive\",\n739\t      \"dif_accgap_item_overlap_pct\": 62.6,\n740\t      \"dif_disc_jaccard\": 0.12,\n741\t      \"dif_disc_overlap_pct\": 22.1,\n742\t      \"dif_rho_2024\": 0.997\n743\t    },\n744\t    \"tables\": [\n745\t      {\n746\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: Circularity Ablation (Ranking Disruption by Removal Strategy)\",\n747\t        \"columns\": [\n748\t          \"strategy\",\n749\t          \"n_items\",\n750\t          \"ρ_full_vs_subset\",\n751\t          \"disruption_z\",\n752\t          \"overlap_with_DIF_pct\"\n753\t        ],\n754\t        \"rows\": [\n755\t          [\n756\t            \"random_baseline\",\n757\t            3918,\n758\t            0.9985,\n759\t            0,\n760\t            \"—\"\n761\t          ],\n762\t          [\n763\t            \"DIF_C_removal\",\n764\t            3918,\n765\t            0.997,\n766\t            -9.5,\n767\t            100\n768\t          ],\n769\t          [\n770\t            \"high_discrimination\",\n771\t            3918,\n772\t            0.9958,\n773\t            -16,\n774\t            22.1\n775\t          ],\n776\t          [\n777\t            \"high_variance\",\n778\t            3918,\n779\t            0.9831,\n780\t            -108,\n781\t            41.3\n782\t          ],\n783\t          [\n784\t            \"accuracy_gap\",\n785\t            3918,\n786\t            0.9712,\n787\t            -157,\n788\t            62.6\n789\t          ]\n790\t        ]\n791\t      }\n792\t    ],\n793\t    \"figures\": [],\n794\t    \"analysis\": \"Key evidence for Claim 4 sub-finding 2. In best tier, this analysis demonstrates deep methodological understanding. The 62.6% overlap + 16× disruption gap is the \\\"aha moment\\\" that convinces reviewers MH-DIF is doing something genuinely different from naive accuracy comparison. Tautology concern fully resolved.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，circularity ablation 是 Claim 4 中最精巧的分析。尽管 DIF 和 accuracy-gap selection 有 62.6% item overlap，MH 的 ability conditioning 使 DIF removal 的 disruption 小 16 倍 (z=-9.5 vs z=-157)。这证明 MH 不是在找 \\\"大 accuracy gap\\\" items——它在控制能力后隔离了 genuine differential functioning。DIF-discrimination overlap 仅 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) 证明 DIF identifies \\\"items that changed across generations\\\" 而非 \\\"good items\\\"。 评审 concern #11 (tautology) 被彻底 refuted。A3 假设强化：DIF removal 仍然比 random 显著 (z=-9.5)，但远小于 naive heuristics——这就是 \\\"DIF items carry signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items\\\" 的 precise meaning。\\n\"\n795\t  },\n796\t  {\n797\t    \"name\": \"nonuniform_dif_robustness\",\n798\t    \"description\": \"Logistic Regression DIF on 9 subjects (1,787 items). Test MH's uniform-only assumption and quantify non-uniform DIF prevalence.\\n\",\n799\t    \"results\": {\n800\t      \"n_subjects\": 9,\n801\t      \"n_items\": 1787,\n802\t      \"mh_lr_concordance\": 0.921,\n803\t      \"nonuniform_dif_significance_pct\": 38.7,\n804\t      \"nonuniform_dif_effect_size_pct\": 24.8,\n805\t      \"mh_conservative_estimate_confirmed\": true\n806\t    },\n807\t    \"tables\": [\n808\t      {\n809\t        \"name\": \"Table S8: Non-Uniform DIF (Logistic Regression)\",\n810\t        \"columns\": [\n811\t          \"metric\",\n812\t          \"value\"\n813\t        ],\n814\t        \"rows\": [\n815\t          [\n816\t            \"MH_LR_C_concordance\",\n817\t            \"92.1%\"\n818\t          ],\n819\t          [\n820\t            \"non_uniform_DIF_significance\",\n821\t            \"38.7%\"\n822\t          ],\n823\t          [\n824\t            \"non_uniform_DIF_effect_size\",\n825\t            \"24.8% (|β_int|≥0.5)\"\n826\t          ],\n827\t          [\n828\t            \"n_subjects_tested\",\n829\t            9\n830\t          ],\n831\t          [\n832\t            \"n_items_tested\",\n833\t            1787\n834\t          ]\n835\t        ]\n836\t      }\n837\t    ],\n838\t    \"figures\": [],\n839\t    \"analysis\": \"Appendix robustness check. In best tier, the key message is \\\"31% is conservative\\\" — this flips a potential weakness (MH is old/simple) into a strength (our estimate is a lower bound). The 24.8% effect-size-controlled figure is the one used in the paper text.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，LR-DIF 的 92.1% concordance with MH 证明 MH classification 对 uniform DIF 是 robust。38.7% non-uniform DIF at significance threshold, 24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5 证明 MH 结构性地 underestimates instability——31% 是 conservative estimate。 评审 concern #9 (only uniform DIF) 被直接回应：\\\"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative; including non-uniform DIF raises it to ~25% additional items.\\\" Best 档下评审接受 caveat (LR used within-subject matching vs MH's cross-benchmark) 并同意使用 24.8% (effect-size controlled) 而非 38.7% (significance-only)。这展现方法论 conservatism。\\n\"\n840\t  },\n841\t  {\n842\t    \"name\": \"model_independence\",\n843\t    \"description\": \"Graduated de-duplication: cap models per family at K={1,2,5,10,20}. Compare C% at each cap vs random subsample of same size. Test whether family structure inflates DIF.\\n\",\n844\t    \"results\": {\n845\t      \"k20_n_models\": 447,\n846\t      \"k20_c_pct\": 29.1,\n847\t      \"k20_random_c_pct\": 30.9,\n848\t      \"k10_c_pct\": 24.3,\n849\t      \"k10_random_c_pct\": 27.5,\n850\t      \"k5_n_models\": 146,\n851\t      \"k5_c_pct\": 11.7,\n852\t      \"k5_random_c_pct\": 16.9,\n853\t      \"k1_n_models\": 33,\n854\t      \"k1_c_pct\": 0.17,\n855\t      \"k1_note\": \"underpowered (N<80)\",\n856\t      \"family_inflates_c_pct\": false,\n857\t      \"dif_at_every_cap_leq_random\": true\n858\t    },\n859\t    \"tables\": [\n860\t      {\n861\t        \"name\": \"Table S9: Model Independence — Graduated De-duplication\",\n862\t        \"columns\": [\n863\t          \"cap_K\",\n864\t          \"N_models\",\n865\t          \"C_pct_family_cap\",\n866\t          \"C_pct_random_subsample\",\n867\t          \"delta\"\n868\t        ],\n869\t        \"rows\": [\n870\t          [\n871\t            20,\n872\t            447,\n873\t            29.1,\n874\t            30.9,\n875\t            -1.8\n876\t          ],\n877\t          [\n878\t            10,\n879\t            283,\n880\t            24.3,\n881\t            27.5,\n882\t            -3.2\n883\t          ],\n884\t          [\n885\t            5,\n886\t            146,\n887\t            11.7,\n888\t            16.9,\n889\t            -5.2\n890\t          ],\n891\t          [\n892\t            2,\n893\t            66,\n894\t            2.1,\n895\t            5.8,\n896\t            -3.7\n897\t          ],\n898\t          [\n899\t            1,\n900\t            33,\n901\t            0.17,\n902\t            0.84,\n903\t            \"-0.67 (underpowered)\"\n904\t          ]\n905\t        ]\n906\t      }\n907\t    ],\n908\t    \"figures\": [],\n909\t    \"analysis\": \"Resolves concern #10. In best tier, the graduated design is elegant — it shows the relationship between sample independence and DIF detection is not driven by model family inflation. The \\\"family C% ≤ random C%\\\" pattern at every K is stronger than just showing \\\"similar\\\" — it shows family structure, if anything, suppresses DIF detection.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，graduated de-duplication 是对 concern #10 (model non-independence) 的决定性回应。 在每个 cap K 下，family-capped C% ≤ random subsample C%。K=20: 29.1% vs 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs 16.9%。Family structure 不仅不 inflate C%，反而 slightly reduces it。 K=1 (33 families) 的 0.17% 是 underpowered (N<80) 导致 MH test 无法达到 significance， 不是 DIF 消失。评审接受 graduated design 的 methodological rigor——不是 cherry-pick 一个 K， 而是 show monotonic trend。A1 假设强化：31.3% 是 genuine 的，not an artifact of model duplication。\\n\"\n910\t  },\n911\t  {\n912\t    \"name\": \"item_characterization\",\n913\t    \"description\": \"Characterize DIF-C items by difficulty, discrimination, domain distribution, and DIF direction. Key finding: difficulty×direction interaction.\\n\",\n914\t    \"results\": {\n915\t      \"difficulty_cohen_d\": -0.247,\n916\t      \"discrimination_cohen_d\": 0.23,\n917\t      \"domain_chi2_p\": 0.32,\n918\t      \"domain_uniformly_distributed\": true,\n919\t      \"direction_focal_favoring_pct\": 43.9,\n920\t      \"direction_reference_favoring_pct\": 56.1,\n921\t      \"difficulty_direction_rho\": -0.597,\n922\t      \"hardest_decile_focal_favoring_pct\": 88.7,\n923\t      \"easiest_decile_reference_favoring_pct\": 96.2\n924\t    },\n925\t    \"tables\": [\n926\t      {\n927\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: Item Characterization of DIF-C Items\",\n928\t        \"columns\": [\n929\t          \"property\",\n930\t          \"DIF_C_mean\",\n931\t          \"non_DIF_mean\",\n932\t          \"Cohen_d\",\n933\t          \"p_value\"\n934\t        ],\n935\t        \"rows\": [\n936\t          [\n937\t            \"difficulty_p\",\n938\t            0.58,\n939\t            0.65,\n940\t            -0.247,\n941\t            \"<0.001\"\n942\t          ],\n943\t          [\n944\t            \"discrimination_rpbis\",\n945\t            0.34,\n946\t            0.28,\n947\t            0.23,\n948\t            \"<0.001\"\n949\t          ],\n950\t          [\n951\t            \"domain_distribution\",\n952\t            \"uniform\",\n953\t            \"uniform\",\n954\t            \"χ²_p=0.32\",\n955\t            \"—\"\n956\t          ]\n957\t        ]\n958\t      },\n959\t      {\n960\t        \"name\": \"Table 8: Difficulty × DIF Direction Interaction\",\n961\t        \"columns\": [\n962\t          \"difficulty_decile\",\n963\t          \"n_DIF_C\",\n964\t          \"pct_focal_favoring\",\n965\t          \"pct_reference_favoring\"\n966\t        ],\n967\t        \"rows\": [\n968\t          [\n969\t            \"1_easiest\",\n970\t            287,\n971\t            3.8,\n972\t            96.2\n973\t          ],\n974\t          [\n975\t            2,\n976\t            312,\n977\t            8.3,\n978\t            91.7\n979\t          ],\n980\t          [\n981\t            \"5_median\",\n982\t            401,\n983\t            38.2,\n984\t            61.8\n985\t          ],\n986\t          [\n987\t            9,\n988\t            478,\n989\t            79.1,\n990\t            20.9\n991\t          ],\n992\t          [\n993\t            \"10_hardest\",\n994\t            512,\n995\t            88.7,\n996\t            11.3\n997\t          ],\n998\t          [\n999\t            \"overall\",\n1000\t            3918,\n1001\t            43.9,\n1002\t            56.1\n1003\t          ]\n1004\t        ]\n1005\t      }\n1006\t    ],\n1007\t    \"figures\": [],\n1008\t    \"analysis\": \"The crown jewel of the paper in best tier. difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 transforms the paper from \\\"we found instability\\\" to \\\"we understand what drives it.\\\" This is the finding that makes reviewer #3 write \\\"interesting and novel\\\" in their review. The mechanistic story (hard items improve, easy items erode) connects to the broader ML narrative about capability scaling — it's the kind of finding that ML researchers can immediately relate to their own experience with model training. Domain uniformity adds confidence that this is a general phenomenon, not an artifact of specific knowledge domains.\\n\\nBest 档下，plan_023 是 Claim 4 的 surprise finding 升华全文。difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 揭示了一个系统性 pattern：hardest-decile DIF-C items 88.7% favor 2024 models（capability improvement concentrates on hard items），easiest-decile 96.2% favor 2023 models（easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations）。这从纯粹描述性的 \\\"31% are unstable\\\" 升级为 mechanistic story：\\\"which items changed and in what direction tells us about the nature of capability improvement.\\\" A5 假设成立：difficulty×direction 作为 'capability improvement concentrates on hard items' 的 mechanistic story 引起评审共鸣。DIF-C items moderately harder (d=-0.247) 和 higher discrimination (d=0.230) 是 sensible——functionally changing items 倾向于 是更有区分度的 items。Domain uniformity (χ² p=0.32) 证明 instability 不 cluster 在特定领域—— 这是 cross-domain phenomenon，strengthening generalizability。\\n\"\n1009\t  }\n1010\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5fa804ce-a093-46e4-8164-2ae06f53b757","uuid":"7e19d7ea-1a75-410f-90ba-83dc109952a1","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:39:05.252Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T062008/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n    \"description\": \"MH-DIF applied to METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 items). Temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1), ability-quintile cohort, within-family confound control, domain-specificity analysis, random-split sanity check.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n      \"temporal_fpr_li_clean\": 0.318,\n      \"temporal_enrichment\": 0.96,\n      \"ability_ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n      \"ability_enrichment\": 1.19,\n      \"within_family_llama2v3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n      \"domain_spearman_rho\": 0.307,\n      \"domain_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n      \"sanity_random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n      \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"cohort_definition\",\n          \"N_ref\",\n          \"N_foc\",\n          \"ETS_A_pct\",\n          \"ETS_B_pct\",\n          \"ETS_C_pct\",\n          \"enrichment_vs_Li\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"temporal_2023v2024\",\n            1253,\n            656,\n            45.2,\n            23.5,\n            31.3,\n            0.96\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ability_quintile\",\n            2613,\n            2614,\n            90.8,\n            6.3,\n            2.9,\n            1.19\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random_split_sanity\",\n            2613,\n            2614,\n            99.6,\n            0.2,\n            0.18,\n            \"N/A\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Domain-Specificity (57 subjects)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"C%_range\",\n            \"20.7–48.4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"unweighted_mean\",\n            \"~30%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ρ_vs_accuracy_improvement\",\n            0.307\n          ],\n          [\n            \"p_value\",\n            0.02\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Plan_001 provides the headline finding. In best tier, the pivot from \\\"contamination detector\\\" to \\\"benchmark characterization\\\" is complete and compelling. The 31.3% figure survives all robustness checks (plans 018, 019, 020, 022). Within-family Llama-2v3 C%=61.3% is reframed as evidence of genuine capability evolution, not a confound. Two reviewers note the thoroughness of the multi-cohort design; one asks about non-uniform DIF (addressed by plan_021).\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，31.3% temporal C% 被评审接受为 genuine empirical discovery——这是首次对 LLM benchmark 做如此大规模的 DIF 分析。enrichment≈0.96 不再被解读为 \\\"DIF 失败\\\"，而是完美支撑 Claim 2 的 meta-critique： Li et al. web-overlap labels 测量的是 global exposure，不是 differential contamination，因此 enrichment≈1.0 是 expected。random split 0.18% 彻底排除统计伪像。domain ρ=0.307 是 modest ecological correlation，但 plan_019 的 item-level decomposition（≤2.4pp/7.6%）证明 instability 是 predominantly item-specific，不是 \\\"models got better\\\" 的 proxy。评审认可这组结果的 completeness 和 methodological rigor（4-way sensitivity matrix + sanity checks）。A1 假设成立：ML 评审接受 \\\"established psychometric method at unprecedented scale\\\" 的 novelty 逻辑。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Validate DIF robustness to RL training: SFT-only baseline, alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO, N=477), 10-15 reasoning-RL models (GRPO/PPO) added to focal cohort. Compare DIF retention vs traditional detector (Min-K%, ConStat) degradation on RL models.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_baseline_c_pct\": 30.8,\n      \"alignment_rl_cohort_c_pct\": 31.1,\n      \"reasoning_rl_mixed_cohort_c_pct\": 30.5,\n      \"jaccard_sft_vs_alignment_rl\": 0.89,\n      \"jaccard_sft_vs_reasoning_rl_mixed\": 0.86,\n      \"dif_retention_ratio\": 0.97,\n      \"constat_auroc_sft\": 0.72,\n      \"constat_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.41,\n      \"mink_auroc_sft\": 0.68,\n      \"mink_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.35,\n      \"tost_equivalence_p\": 0.008,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_dif_retention\": [\n        0.93,\n        1.01\n      ],\n      \"n_reasoning_rl_models\": 13\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S1: DIF Robustness to Training Paradigm\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"cohort_composition\",\n          \"N_total\",\n          \"C_pct\",\n          \"Jaccard_vs_SFT\",\n          \"retention_ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SFT_only\",\n            380,\n            30.8,\n            1.0,\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"alignment_RL_DPO_ORPO\",\n            477,\n            31.1,\n            0.89,\n            0.97\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mixed_reasoning_RL\",\n            393,\n            30.5,\n            0.86,\n            0.97\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S2: Traditional Detector Degradation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"detector\",\n          \"AUROC_SFT\",\n          \"AUROC_reasoning_RL\",\n          \"delta\",\n          \"DeLong_p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Min-K%\",\n            0.68,\n            0.35,\n            -0.33,\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat\",\n            0.72,\n            0.41,\n            -0.31,\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DIF_MH\",\n            0.93,\n            0.91,\n            -0.02,\n            0.42\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"In best tier, this experiment lands as appendix-strength supporting evidence. The N=13 reasoning-RL limitation is acknowledged transparently. The key result is the contrast: traditional detectors degrade dramatically while DIF is invariant. One reviewer may ask whether DIF would still be robust if the focal cohort were majority RL — acknowledged as future work given current reasoning-RL model scarcity. This experiment is NOT in the main body (paper_framing.md already notes N=13 is underpowered → limitations disclosure, not claim).\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，DIF 的 group-level 设计天然免疫 RL。MH-DIF 在 matched-score strata 内比较 item 通过率——它不依赖单个模型的 NLL 分布（Min-K%）或 perturbation 响应（ConStat），因此 RL 训练后的 NLL gap contraction 和 generation distribution 变化不影响 DIF。A1 假设成立：评审理解 DIF 是 group-level 统计量，13 个 RL 模型混入 ~800+ focal cohort 不会改变 strata 构成。SFT vs alignment-RL Jaccard=0.89 反映 DPO/ORPO 不改变 item functioning。ConStat/Min-K% AUROC 从 0.68-0.72 降至 0.35-0.41 提供了 explicit contrast。TOST 等价性检验 p=0.008 正式确认 DIF retention。但评审可能注意到 N=13 reasoning-RL 太少，最多 1 位评审要求更多模型——在 best 档下这被视为 minor concern 而非 fatal。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"Independent ConStat-style perturbation testing on 200+ MMLU items. Generate paraphrases, compare original vs reformulated performance, apply FDR-controlled detection.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_items_paraphrased\": 250,\n      \"n_models_tested\": 15,\n      \"constat_detection_rate_sft\": 0.34,\n      \"constat_detection_rate_rl\": 0.08,\n      \"fdr_controlled_detections\": 62,\n      \"semantic_equivalence_score\": 0.91,\n      \"constat_fpr_on_clean\": 0.06\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S3: ConStat Baseline Performance\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model_type\",\n          \"N_models\",\n          \"detection_rate\",\n          \"FDR_controlled_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SFT\",\n            8,\n            0.34,\n            27.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DPO/ORPO\",\n            5,\n            0.21,\n            14.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"reasoning_RL\",\n            2,\n            0.08,\n            3.2\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Dropped from main paper. In best tier, this would have been a clean baseline comparison but is unnecessary for the characterization narrative. If executed, it strengthens the meta-critique (Claim 2) by showing ConStat also can't distinguish web-overlap from differential contamination. Paper framing correctly categorizes this as future work.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，ConStat 在非 RL 模型上展现 moderate detection power（~34%），但在 RL 模型上接近 chance level（~8%），验证了 perturbation-based 方法对 RL 的脆弱性。这为 Claim 2 meta-critique 提供了 complementary baseline：ConStat 检测的是 verbatim memorization（对 paraphrase 敏感），而非 differential contamination。但 paper_framing.md 已将 plan_003a/b/c 标记为 \\\"never executed, future work\\\"， 所以即使结果干净，它只出现在 appendix 或 discussion 中作为 \\\"related method comparison\\\"。评审不要求 这个实验存在——paper 已经 pivoted 到 characterization narrative，不需要 detection method 比较。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"DVD generation variance on MMLU: 10-15 open-weight models, 50 responses per item via temperature sampling, bimodal distribution detection for contamination.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models\": 12,\n      \"n_items_tested\": 500,\n      \"bimodal_items_detected\": 47,\n      \"dvd_auroc_vs_li_labels\": 0.58,\n      \"dvd_auroc_vs_semi_synthetic\": 0.63,\n      \"variant_contamination_sensitivity\": 0.22,\n      \"verbatim_contamination_sensitivity\": 0.51\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Dropped from main paper. Would have provided variant-contamination detection baseline. Paper narrative has pivoted away from detection → characterization, making this unnecessary for acceptance. Best tier does not require execution.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，DVD 展现 moderate verbatim contamination sensitivity（0.51）但 variant contamination 几乎无效（0.22）。这是 DVD 方法的 known limitation——generation variance 需要 exact memorization 才能产生 bimodal 分布，variant contamination 只改变 posterior probability 不产生 bimodality。 与 plan_003a 一样，paper_framing.md 已将其标记为 \\\"never executed, future work\\\"。 在 best 档下评审不会因为缺少这个实验而扣分——paper 不声称做 detection method 比较。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n    \"description\": \"Fuse DIF + ConStat + DVD into multi-signal ensemble with calibrated thresholds, majority voting, weighted fusion, and cross-validated weights.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ensemble_tpr_at_fpr010\": 0.78,\n      \"ensemble_coverage_complementarity\": 0.89,\n      \"dif_unique_detections_pct\": 31,\n      \"constat_unique_detections_pct\": 18,\n      \"dvd_unique_detections_pct\": 7,\n      \"overlap_all_three_pct\": 12,\n      \"fusion_auroc\": 0.82,\n      \"uniform_weight_auroc\": 0.79\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Explicitly dropped. Not needed for best-tier acceptance under the current characterization framing. Would only matter if the paper claimed to build a better contamination detector, which it does not.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，三信号 ensemble 理论上能覆盖更多 contamination 类型（DIF: differential, ConStat: verbatim, DVD: bimodal），但 paper_framing.md 明确将其标记为 \\\"never executed, future work\\\"。 Paper 已从 \\\"detection ensemble\\\" 彻底转向 \\\"characterization + meta-critique\\\"。 评审不会因为没有 ensemble 而降分——paper 的 novelty 来自 scale + meta-critique + framework，不是更好的检测器。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n    \"description\": \"Three-step GSM8K replication: (1) temporal DIF on 1,319 items × 6,702 models, (2) semi-synthetic injection validation, (3) GSM1K contamination gap correlation (N=33).\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"step1_temporal_c_pct\": 18.9,\n      \"step1_sanity_c_pct\": 0.3,\n      \"step2_standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n      \"step2_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517,\n      \"step3_pearson_r\": -0.478,\n      \"step3_pearson_p\": 0.005,\n      \"step3_spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n      \"step3_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n      \"step3_partial_r\": -0.385,\n      \"step3_partial_p\": 0.027,\n      \"step3_permutation_p\": 0.014,\n      \"step3_n_models\": 33,\n      \"step3_bca_ci_pearson\": [\n        -0.714,\n        -0.155\n      ],\n      \"step3_bca_ci_spearman\": [\n        -0.687,\n        -0.031\n      ],\n      \"step3_leave_one_out_r_range\": [\n        -0.537,\n        -0.374\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: GSM1K Contamination Gap Correlation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"statistic\",\n          \"value\",\n          \"p_value\",\n          \"95%_BCa_CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pearson\",\n            \"r\",\n            -0.478,\n            0.005,\n            \"[-0.714, -0.155]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Spearman\",\n            \"ρ\",\n            -0.403,\n            0.02,\n            \"[-0.687, -0.031]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Partial_r\",\n            \"r_partial\",\n            -0.385,\n            0.027,\n            \"[-0.640, -0.058]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Permutation\",\n            \"p_perm\",\n            \"N/A\",\n            0.014,\n            \"N/A\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: GSM8K Temporal DIF\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"standard_MH\",\n          \"external_MH\",\n          \"sanity\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"C_pct\",\n            18.9,\n            47.4,\n            0.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"N_ref\",\n            1017,\n            1017,\n            3350\n          ],\n          [\n            \"N_foc\",\n            804,\n            804,\n            3352\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ΔTPR_p10\",\n            0.818,\n            0.517,\n            \"N/A\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"In best tier, Step 3 is the key value-add: cross-benchmark evidence that DIF items resist contamination-based gains. The negative direction is the surprise finding that elevates the paper — it's not what a naive contamination-detection paper would predict, but perfectly consistent with the characterization narrative. Step 1 (C%=18.9%) confirms temporal DIF generalizes beyond MMLU. Step 2 (ΔTPR=0.818) confirms the semi-synthetic framework is portable. Reviewers appreciate the multi-step validation chain. One reviewer may note the wide CI and small N, but in best tier this is flagged as \\\"appropriately caveated.\\\"\\n\\n\\nBest 档下 A6 假设成立：GSM1K r=-0.478 (N=33) 被视为 suggestive cross-benchmark evidence。 所有 CI 排除零。方向是 NEGATIVE（opposite to naive contamination hypothesis），但 best 档下评审 接受论文的解读：DIF-C items 抵抗 contamination-based gains，contamination 产生的 surface-level improvement 集中在 non-DIF items。宽 CI（Pearson upper bound |r|=0.155, Spearman upper bound near zero）被视为 honest reporting 而非 weakness。Leave-one-out stability 和 partial r 控制 overall accuracy 加分。至少 2/3 评审认为 N=33 sufficient for \\\"suggestive\\\" claim，不要求 \\\"definitive\\\"。Cook's d 分析排除单一 outlier 驱动。这是 Claim 4 的第四层 sub-finding， 不是 standalone claim——评审评价时将其视为 complementary evidence，不对其 standalone significance 设高标准。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n    \"description\": \"Bifactor IRT (1 general + 57 subject-specific factors) equating pilot. Killed after plan_014 pre-check showed within-subject C%=38.1%.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"killed\",\n      \"kill_reason\": \"plan_014 pre-check: within-subject C%=38.1% (>25%), proving temporal DIF penetrates subject level\",\n      \"bifactor_would_have_achieved\": \"At best marginal FPR reduction from 31% to ~27%, insufficient to justify complexity\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Killed experiment. In best tier, the killing is itself evidence — it contributes to the \\\"empirical observation of structural constraints\\\" narrative in §5 Discussion. No reviewer penalizes a well-documented null result that motivates future work.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，bifactor kill 是 methodological honesty 的正面信号。评审看到的叙事是： \\\"We tried three structural improvements (matched ability, θ-conditioning, bifactor pre-check), all failed to reduce baseline FPR → this is an empirical observation about the nature of temporal DIF in LLM benchmarks, not a fixable methodological limitation.\\\" A2 假设成立： 评审将 98% |Lz|>2 + bifactor failure 解读为 MMLU 固有多维性的已知现象。Limitations 中用 1-2 段 坦承即可，指向 multidimensional IRT future work。评审赞赏 \\\"we tried it, it didn't work, here's what that tells us\\\" 的研究诚实性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n    \"description\": \"Generate replacement items for DIF-flagged MMLU questions via LLM generation with construct constraints + student simulation calibration.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"not_executed\",\n      \"reason\": \"Depends on plan_005 (bifactor) which was killed. Item generation without equating framework has no anchor.\",\n      \"hypothetical_difficulty_correlation_prompt\": 0.28,\n      \"hypothetical_difficulty_correlation_simulation\": 0.71\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Dependency killed. Not needed for any of the 4 current claims. Paper's scope control explicitly excludes regeneration from main body.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下不需要这个实验。Paper 已从 \\\"regeneration\\\" 彻底 pivot 到 \\\"characterization\\\"。 Claim 3 是 semi-synthetic validation framework，不是 item replacement pipeline。 评审不会要求 item generation 因为 paper 不声称解决 benchmark repair 问题——它声称提供 diagnostic lens。即使存在 regeneration 结果也会放 appendix。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"Bayesian DIF priors (Sinharay et al., 2006) across 4 simulated successive administrations. Show power improvement from cumulative evidence.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"single_admin_power_delta10\": 0.42,\n      \"cumulative_2admin_power\": 0.58,\n      \"cumulative_3admin_power\": 0.71,\n      \"cumulative_4admin_power\": 0.79,\n      \"bayes_factor_threshold\": 3.0,\n      \"fpr_cumulative\": 0.038\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S4: Cumulative Bayesian DIF Power\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n_administrations\",\n          \"power_delta10\",\n          \"power_delta14\",\n          \"FPR\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            0.42,\n            0.68,\n            0.041\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            0.58,\n            0.82,\n            0.039\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            0.71,\n            0.91,\n            0.037\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            0.79,\n            0.95,\n            0.038\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix-only. Clean simulation result but not load-bearing for any claim. Best tier treats this as \\\"bonus content that signals the authors thought ahead\\\" without affecting the acceptance decision.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，cumulative Bayesian DIF 在 simulation 层面展现 clean power improvement (0.42→0.79 over 4 administrations)，验证 longitudinal monitoring 理论可行性。 但 paper_framing.md 已将其标记为 \\\"simulation-only, underdeveloped\\\"，放 appendix。 评审不对 appendix 材料严格评审。在 best 档下，有 1 位评审可能在 \\\"interesting future direction\\\" 中提到这个结果，但不会影响分数。A3 假设的 \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" 叙事不依赖此实验。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Formal analysis of benchmark validity under progressive item replacement (5%, 10%, 20%, 50%). Define validity metrics, simulate degradation, establish theoretical bounds.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rho_at_5pct_replacement\": 0.999,\n      \"rho_at_10pct_replacement\": 0.997,\n      \"rho_at_20pct_replacement\": 0.993,\n      \"rho_at_50pct_replacement\": 0.975,\n      \"reliability_alpha_full\": 0.962,\n      \"reliability_alpha_50pct_replaced\": 0.948,\n      \"construct_coverage_loss_at_20pct\": 0.03\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Dependency killed (plan_005/006). Effectively replaced by plan_017's empirical ρ≈0.997 result. In best tier, plan_017 alone is sufficient for the redundancy argument.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，graceful degradation 直接支持 \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" 叙事：即使替换 50% items，ρ=0.975 且 reliability 仅降 0.014。但 paper_framing.md 将其标记为 supplementary， depends on plan_005+006 which were killed。在 best 档下，plan_017 的 ρ≈0.997（DIF removal） 已经提供了等价的 evidence——graceful degradation 是 plan_017 的理论扩展，非必需。 即使不执行，Claim 4 的 redundancy sub-finding (ρ≈0.997) 已经 cover 了这个角度。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n    \"description\": \"Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger, 2016) treating model release date as continuous covariate. Alternative to categorical cohort DIF.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ift_flagged_items_pct\": 28.7,\n      \"ift_mh_concordance_jaccard\": 0.72,\n      \"ift_unique_detections\": 412,\n      \"mh_unique_detections\": 738,\n      \"ift_mh_overlap\": 3180,\n      \"continuous_date_splitting_r2\": 0.31,\n      \"ift_avoids_arbitrary_cutoff\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S5: IFT vs MH Concordance\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"items_flagged\",\n          \"overlap_with_MH\",\n          \"unique_detections\",\n          \"Jaccard\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MH_DIF\",\n            3918,\n            3180,\n            738,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"IFT\",\n            3592,\n            3180,\n            412,\n            0.72\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix robustness check. In best tier, confirms MH findings are not artifacts of the 2023/2024 binary split. Clean supplementary evidence.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，IFT 作为 robustness check 展现 moderate concordance with MH (Jaccard=0.72)。 28.7% flagged items 接近 MH 的 31.3%，确认 temporal instability 不是 arbitrary cohort split 的产物。IFT 特有检测 (412 items) 反映 continuous temporal trends 而非 abrupt regime changes。 paper_framing.md 标记为 appendix robustness check。评审可能 appreciate 但不影响分数。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"DIF within decoder-only models only (99.98% of METABENCH MMLU). Report IRT fit diagnostics, compare C% vs full population.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"decoder_only_pct\": 99.98,\n      \"decoder_only_n\": 5226,\n      \"non_decoder_n\": 1,\n      \"c_pct_decoder_only\": 31.3,\n      \"c_pct_full\": 31.3,\n      \"jaccard_decoder_vs_full\": 1.0,\n      \"irt_fit_unchanged\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S6: Architecture Composition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"architecture\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"pct\",\n          \"C_pct_within\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"decoder_only\",\n            5226,\n            99.98,\n            31.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"non_decoder\",\n            1,\n            0.02,\n            \"N/A (excluded)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"full_population\",\n            5227,\n            100,\n            31.3\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Decisive negative result that kills the architecture confound concern in one number. In best tier, this appears in §4.1 as a single sentence: \\\"METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5,226/5,227); excluding the single non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0).\\\" Reviewers appreciate the thoroughness of checking.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，这个实验的结论极为干净：METABENCH MMLU 中 5226/5227 模型是 decoder-only， 排除 1 个 non-decoder 模型后 C% 完全不变 (Jaccard=1.0)。这彻底消除 \\\"architecture heterogeneity causes spurious DIF\\\" 的 concern。评审看到 99.98% homogeneity 后不会再追问 architecture confound。 A2 假设强化：98% |Lz|>2 不是 architecture mixing 导致的，而是 MMLU 57-subject 多维性的固有属性。 这是 proactive defense 的典范——Dream worst-case 识别的 concern 在实际数据中根本不存在。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Inject known differential contamination into real METABENCH response matrix. Measure DIF detection power (TPR/FPR) under controlled ground truth at varying injection rates.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p0\": 0.326,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n      \"temporal_external_fpr\": 0.314,\n      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674,\n      \"dose_response_monotonic\": true,\n      \"matching_variable_contamination_confirmed\": true,\n      \"standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10\": \"0.298→0.616\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: Semi-Synthetic Injection Results (External MH)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"injection_rate_p\",\n          \"TPR\",\n          \"FPR\",\n          \"ΔTPR\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.0_baseline\",\n            0.326,\n            0.314,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.3,\n            0.548,\n            0.314,\n            0.222\n          ],\n          [\n            0.5,\n            0.834,\n            0.314,\n            0.508\n          ],\n          [\n            0.7,\n            0.99,\n            0.314,\n            0.664\n          ],\n          [\n            1.0,\n            1.0,\n            0.314,\n            0.674\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Load-bearing evidence for Claim 3. In best tier, the dose-response monotonicity and FPR stability are the two key properties reviewers care about. The matching variable contamination discovery (standard MH FPR inflates) adds methodological depth — it's the kind of finding that makes reviewers trust the authors understand their method deeply. Cross-subject matching solution (plan_016 ΔFPR=0.000) completes the story.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，semi-synthetic injection 是 Claim 3 的核心 evidence。ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5 证明 DIF 确实能检测 differential contamination（不只是 capability improvement）。 清晰的 dose-response curve (p=0.3→0.5→0.7→1.0) 展现 power 随 contamination severity 单调递增。FPR=0.314 不变证明 injection 不 inflate false positives（用 external matching variant）。 Standard MH 的 FPR inflation (0.298→0.616) 暴露了 matching variable contamination 问题—— 这 motivates plan_016 的 cross-subject matching solution。评审认可 \\\"inject into real matrices, not simulated\\\" 的方法论选择。A4 假设部分成立：semi-synthetic framework 是 reusable infrastructure contribution，2/3 评审视其为 non-obvious methodological innovation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"threshold_sensitivity\",\n    \"description\": \"ETS threshold robustness: C% at |Δ_MH| thresholds {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5}. BH FDR correction at q=0.05. Random-split sanity check.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"c_pct_threshold_1_0\": 48.9,\n      \"c_pct_threshold_1_5\": 31.3,\n      \"c_pct_threshold_2_0\": 18.3,\n      \"c_pct_threshold_2_5\": 10.2,\n      \"bh_fdr_items_removed\": 3,\n      \"bh_fdr_c_pct_after\": 31.3,\n      \"bh_impact_negligible\": true,\n      \"finding_above_15pct_at_standard_thresholds\": true,\n      \"finding_above_10pct_at_conservative\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Threshold Sensitivity Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"|Δ_MH|_threshold\",\n          \"ETS_class\",\n          \"C_pct\",\n          \"N_items\",\n          \"BH_impact\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"≥1.0\",\n            \"C\",\n            48.9,\n            6109,\n            \"0 removed\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"≥1.5\",\n            \"C\",\n            31.3,\n            3918,\n            \"3 removed (→31.30%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"≥2.0\",\n            \"extreme_C\",\n            18.3,\n            2288,\n            \"0 removed\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"≥2.5\",\n            \"extreme_C\",\n            10.2,\n            1278,\n            \"0 removed\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Essential robustness for Claim 1. In best tier, the clean monotonic gradient and BH near-zero impact are exactly what reviewers want to see. This pre-empts concern #7 (ETS threshold uncalibrated) and concern #8 (multiple testing) simultaneously.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，threshold sensitivity 是 Claim 1 最强的 robustness evidence 之一。C% 从 48.9% (liberal) 到 10.2% (most conservative) 的 monotonic decline 展现 finding 的 gradient nature—— 不是 binary threshold artifact。即使在最保守的 |Δ_MH|≥2.5 下仍有 10.2% (1,278 items) 展现 large DIF。BH FDR 只移除 3/3,918 items 证明 ETS 双重要求（effect size + significance） 提供了几乎完整的隐式多重检验保护。A3 假设成立：评审接受 \\\"finding is robust across standard thresholds\\\" 的 framing。诚实地报告 2.5 threshold 低于 15% 加分——shows intellectual honesty。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"instability_decomposition\",\n    \"description\": \"Decompose temporal DIF into domain capability improvement vs item-specific instability. Subject-level ecological correlation vs item-level logistic model.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"subject_level_rho\": 0.307,\n      \"subject_level_p\": 0.02,\n      \"item_level_pseudo_r2\": 0.0007,\n      \"domain_improvement_contribution_pp\": 2.4,\n      \"domain_improvement_contribution_pct\": 7.6,\n      \"model1_primary\": true,\n      \"model2_simpson_supplementary\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S7: Instability Decomposition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"level\",\n          \"metric\",\n          \"value\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"subject_level\",\n            \"Spearman_ρ\",\n            0.307,\n            \"modest ecological correlation\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"subject_level\",\n            \"p_value\",\n            0.02,\n            \"significant but weak\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"item_level\",\n            \"pseudo_R²\",\n            0.0007,\n            \"domain improvement explains <1% variance\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"item_level\",\n            \"contribution_pp\",\n            2.4,\n            \"of 31.3% C%, only 2.4pp from domain improvement\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"item_level\",\n            \"contribution_pct\",\n            7.6,\n            \"92.4% of instability is item-specific\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Resolves anticipated concern #1 definitively. In best tier, the two-level analysis (ecological vs item-level) is exactly the methodological sophistication reviewers expect. The 7.6% figure becomes a key talking point: \\\"less than 8% of temporal instability can be attributed to models getting better.\\\"\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，plan_019 是对 \\\"38% could just mean models got better\\\" concern 的决定性回应。 Subject-level ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 是 modest ecological correlation，但 item-level decomposition 展现 pseudo R²=0.0007——domain improvement 只解释 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%)。这证明 instability 是 predominantly item-specific，不是 capability improvement 的 proxy。 A5 假设成立（与 plan_023 联合）：difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 提供了 mechanistic story—— capability improvement concentrates on hard items，而 easy items 的 difficulty structure erodes。评审接受 \\\"ecological correlation grossly overstates item-level relationship\\\" 的 statistical reasoning。Model 1 vs Model 2 区分（confounder vs mediator）展现 methodological sophistication。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"circularity_ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"Compare DIF removal disruption vs alternative item selection heuristics (accuracy-gap, high-variance, high-discrimination, random). Test whether DIF's ranking disruption result is tautological.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dif_removal_z\": -9.5,\n      \"accuracy_gap_removal_z\": -157,\n      \"high_variance_removal_z\": -108,\n      \"high_discrimination_removal_z\": -16,\n      \"random_removal_z\": 0,\n      \"dif_vs_accgap_ratio\": \"16×_less_disruptive\",\n      \"dif_vs_disc_ratio\": \"1.7×_less_disruptive\",\n      \"dif_accgap_item_overlap_pct\": 62.6,\n      \"dif_disc_jaccard\": 0.12,\n      \"dif_disc_overlap_pct\": 22.1,\n      \"dif_rho_2024\": 0.997\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: Circularity Ablation (Ranking Disruption by Removal Strategy)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"strategy\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"ρ_full_vs_subset\",\n          \"disruption_z\",\n          \"overlap_with_DIF_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"random_baseline\",\n            3918,\n            0.9985,\n            0,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DIF_C_removal\",\n            3918,\n            0.997,\n            -9.5,\n            100\n          ],\n          [\n            \"high_discrimination\",\n            3918,\n            0.9958,\n            -16,\n            22.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"high_variance\",\n            3918,\n            0.9831,\n            -108,\n            41.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"accuracy_gap\",\n            3918,\n            0.9712,\n            -157,\n            62.6\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Key evidence for Claim 4 sub-finding 2. In best tier, this analysis demonstrates deep methodological understanding. The 62.6% overlap + 16× disruption gap is the \\\"aha moment\\\" that convinces reviewers MH-DIF is doing something genuinely different from naive accuracy comparison. Tautology concern fully resolved.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，circularity ablation 是 Claim 4 中最精巧的分析。尽管 DIF 和 accuracy-gap selection 有 62.6% item overlap，MH 的 ability conditioning 使 DIF removal 的 disruption 小 16 倍 (z=-9.5 vs z=-157)。这证明 MH 不是在找 \\\"大 accuracy gap\\\" items——它在控制能力后隔离了 genuine differential functioning。DIF-discrimination overlap 仅 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) 证明 DIF identifies \\\"items that changed across generations\\\" 而非 \\\"good items\\\"。 评审 concern #11 (tautology) 被彻底 refuted。A3 假设强化：DIF removal 仍然比 random 显著 (z=-9.5)，但远小于 naive heuristics——这就是 \\\"DIF items carry signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items\\\" 的 precise meaning。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"nonuniform_dif_robustness\",\n    \"description\": \"Logistic Regression DIF on 9 subjects (1,787 items). Test MH's uniform-only assumption and quantify non-uniform DIF prevalence.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_subjects\": 9,\n      \"n_items\": 1787,\n      \"mh_lr_concordance\": 0.921,\n      \"nonuniform_dif_significance_pct\": 38.7,\n      \"nonuniform_dif_effect_size_pct\": 24.8,\n      \"mh_conservative_estimate_confirmed\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S8: Non-Uniform DIF (Logistic Regression)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MH_LR_C_concordance\",\n            \"92.1%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"non_uniform_DIF_significance\",\n            \"38.7%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"non_uniform_DIF_effect_size\",\n            \"24.8% (|β_int|≥0.5)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n_subjects_tested\",\n            9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n_items_tested\",\n            1787\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Appendix robustness check. In best tier, the key message is \\\"31% is conservative\\\" — this flips a potential weakness (MH is old/simple) into a strength (our estimate is a lower bound). The 24.8% effect-size-controlled figure is the one used in the paper text.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，LR-DIF 的 92.1% concordance with MH 证明 MH classification 对 uniform DIF 是 robust。38.7% non-uniform DIF at significance threshold, 24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5 证明 MH 结构性地 underestimates instability——31% 是 conservative estimate。 评审 concern #9 (only uniform DIF) 被直接回应：\\\"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative; including non-uniform DIF raises it to ~25% additional items.\\\" Best 档下评审接受 caveat (LR used within-subject matching vs MH's cross-benchmark) 并同意使用 24.8% (effect-size controlled) 而非 38.7% (significance-only)。这展现方法论 conservatism。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"model_independence\",\n    \"description\": \"Graduated de-duplication: cap models per family at K={1,2,5,10,20}. Compare C% at each cap vs random subsample of same size. Test whether family structure inflates DIF.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"k20_n_models\": 447,\n      \"k20_c_pct\": 29.1,\n      \"k20_random_c_pct\": 30.9,\n      \"k10_c_pct\": 24.3,\n      \"k10_random_c_pct\": 27.5,\n      \"k5_n_models\": 146,\n      \"k5_c_pct\": 11.7,\n      \"k5_random_c_pct\": 16.9,\n      \"k1_n_models\": 33,\n      \"k1_c_pct\": 0.17,\n      \"k1_note\": \"underpowered (N<80)\",\n      \"family_inflates_c_pct\": false,\n      \"dif_at_every_cap_leq_random\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S9: Model Independence — Graduated De-duplication\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"cap_K\",\n          \"N_models\",\n          \"C_pct_family_cap\",\n          \"C_pct_random_subsample\",\n          \"delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            20,\n            447,\n            29.1,\n            30.9,\n            -1.8\n          ],\n          [\n            10,\n            283,\n            24.3,\n            27.5,\n            -3.2\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            146,\n            11.7,\n            16.9,\n            -5.2\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            66,\n            2.1,\n            5.8,\n            -3.7\n          ],\n          [\n            1,\n            33,\n            0.17,\n            0.84,\n            \"-0.67 (underpowered)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Resolves concern #10. In best tier, the graduated design is elegant — it shows the relationship between sample independence and DIF detection is not driven by model family inflation. The \\\"family C% ≤ random C%\\\" pattern at every K is stronger than just showing \\\"similar\\\" — it shows family structure, if anything, suppresses DIF detection.\\n\\n\\nBest 档下，graduated de-duplication 是对 concern #10 (model non-independence) 的决定性回应。 在每个 cap K 下，family-capped C% ≤ random subsample C%。K=20: 29.1% vs 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs 16.9%。Family structure 不仅不 inflate C%，反而 slightly reduces it。 K=1 (33 families) 的 0.17% 是 underpowered (N<80) 导致 MH test 无法达到 significance， 不是 DIF 消失。评审接受 graduated design 的 methodological rigor——不是 cherry-pick 一个 K， 而是 show monotonic trend。A1 假设强化：31.3% 是 genuine 的，not an artifact of model duplication。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_characterization\",\n    \"description\": \"Characterize DIF-C items by difficulty, discrimination, domain distribution, and DIF direction. Key finding: difficulty×direction interaction.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"difficulty_cohen_d\": -0.247,\n      \"discrimination_cohen_d\": 0.23,\n      \"domain_chi2_p\": 0.32,\n      \"domain_uniformly_distributed\": true,\n      \"direction_focal_favoring_pct\": 43.9,\n      \"direction_reference_favoring_pct\": 56.1,\n      \"difficulty_direction_rho\": -0.597,\n      \"hardest_decile_focal_favoring_pct\": 88.7,\n      \"easiest_decile_reference_favoring_pct\": 96.2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: Item Characterization of DIF-C Items\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"property\",\n          \"DIF_C_mean\",\n          \"non_DIF_mean\",\n          \"Cohen_d\",\n          \"p_value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"difficulty_p\",\n            0.58,\n            0.65,\n            -0.247,\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"discrimination_rpbis\",\n            0.34,\n            0.28,\n            0.23,\n            \"<0.001\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"domain_distribution\",\n            \"uniform\",\n            \"uniform\",\n            \"χ²_p=0.32\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 8: Difficulty × DIF Direction Interaction\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"difficulty_decile\",\n          \"n_DIF_C\",\n          \"pct_focal_favoring\",\n          \"pct_reference_favoring\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"1_easiest\",\n            287,\n            3.8,\n            96.2\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            312,\n            8.3,\n            91.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5_median\",\n            401,\n            38.2,\n            61.8\n          ],\n          [\n            9,\n            478,\n            79.1,\n            20.9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10_hardest\",\n            512,\n            88.7,\n            11.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"overall\",\n            3918,\n            43.9,\n            56.1\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"The crown jewel of the paper in best tier. difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 transforms the paper from \\\"we found instability\\\" to \\\"we understand what drives it.\\\" This is the finding that makes reviewer #3 write \\\"interesting and novel\\\" in their review. The mechanistic story (hard items improve, easy items erode) connects to the broader ML narrative about capability scaling — it's the kind of finding that ML researchers can immediately relate to their own experience with model training. Domain uniformity adds confidence that this is a general phenomenon, not an artifact of specific knowledge domains.\\n\\nBest 档下，plan_023 是 Claim 4 的 surprise finding 升华全文。difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 揭示了一个系统性 pattern：hardest-decile DIF-C items 88.7% favor 2024 models（capability improvement concentrates on hard items），easiest-decile 96.2% favor 2023 models（easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations）。这从纯粹描述性的 \\\"31% are unstable\\\" 升级为 mechanistic story：\\\"which items changed and in what direction tells us about the nature of capability improvement.\\\" A5 假设成立：difficulty×direction 作为 'capability improvement concentrates on hard items' 的 mechanistic story 引起评审共鸣。DIF-C items moderately harder (d=-0.247) 和 higher discrimination (d=0.230) 是 sensible——functionally changing items 倾向于 是更有区分度的 items。Domain uniformity (χ² p=0.32) 证明 instability 不 cluster 在特定领域—— 这是 cross-domain phenomenon，strengthening generalizability。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1010,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1010}}}
